Subject: [PATCH 02583/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A2
 (HEADLINE skeptic-proofing; GATED on exp4392
 localizer_beats_ensemble_baseline==true) -- is the A1 localizer win GENUINE,
 or a synthetic-data artifact? The operator (twice-burned on over-claims) will
 ask: does the localization win come from (a) TEMPLATE-ARTIFACT LEAKAGE (the
 localizer learned the synthetic injection template, not real first-error
 structure -- the win must hold when TRAINED on synthetic but TESTED on REAL
 held-out first-error labels, which A1 already targets; here harden it with a
 template-ablation: shuffle/randomize the injection template and confirm the
 real-split F1 DROPS), (b) POSITION/LENGTH bias (the localizer just predicts
 'the error is at position p' -- test against a content-blind position-only
 baseline built from the empirical first-error-step distribution), or (c)
 SYNTHETIC-DISTRIBUTION OVERFIT (re-test on a held-out REAL split + a second
 seed regime, bootstrap CI95)? This DIAGNOSTIC (no new synthesis infra, no
 live LLM) re-tests the A1 winning localizer three ways. Emit
 localizer_win_is_genuine BARE bool := (the A1 real-split localization
 advantage survives the position-only-baseline control AND degrades under
 template-ablation AND holds on a held-out REAL split, all CI95-excl-0).
 verifier_is_oracle=false. A pass = the localizer headline graduates; a fail =
 the A1 win is artifact-confounded and is QUARANTINED + the residual logged as
 a missing-verifier gap. NO TRM training; CPU-offline.

